      ],
      "anchorLocalId": "jiutangshu:153:p062",
      "ownerFinding": "Unnamed inferred placeholder. s0103 「袁高，字公頤，恕己之孫」 states only that Yuan Gao was Shuji's grandson; the intervening father is never mentioned or quoted. The explicit grandson relation survives (claims 504 and 554). Remove p062; drop intermediaryPersonIds from claims 504 and 554.",
      "ownerDisposition": "accept-hold-propose-remove-inferred-person",
      "independentVerdict": "hold",
      "primaryWitnessUnits": [
        {
          "unitId": "s0103",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/153.json",
          "zh": "袁高，字公頤，恕己之孫。",
          "enLiteral": "Yuan Gao, courtesy name Gongyi, was the grandson of Shuji.",
          "enIdiomatic": "Yuan Gao, courtesy name Gongyi, was the grandson of Shuji."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caseId": "sha256:b311d6c1a344046b9508db3103b49c184c6e1db6fa8cb109430765f1cc9083f3",
      "localId": "jiutangshu:153:p052",
      "canonicalPersonId": "per_C2RF55NX3VYXRSPZQDGR",
      "transportLocalPeople": [
        "jiutangshu:153:p044",
        "jiutangshu:153:p052"
      ],
      "protectedLocalPeople": [
        "jiutangshu:153:p044",
        "jiutangshu:153:p052",
        "jiutangshu:157:p044",
        "jiutangshu:157:p051"
      ],
      "anchorLocalId": "jiutangshu:157:p044",
      "ownerFinding": "Neither a placeholder nor a distinct person: a within-chapter duplicate created at an extraction chunk boundary. p044 is Boqu with explicit 伯芻 surfaces at s0070/s0071/s0077/s0080/s0083. His biography runs straight into s0084 「子寬夫」, whose implied subject is Boqu. p052 repeats Boqu with no surface of its own (its own note: \"Named only in read-only prior units\"). The prepared case already places p044 and p052 under the same canonical person per_C2RF55NX3VYXRSPZQDGR, so merging creates no new identity. Merge p052 into p044: move the parent-of Kuanfu (s0084) and Duanfu (s0097) relations to p044, and drop p052's duplicate sex, historicity, polity and AD 815 attestation (p044 claims 338/339/340/346 carry them explicitly). After the merge, p044 supplies the admissible primary witness 「伯芻」 (s0071 「伯芻，字素芝」) for this case.",
      "ownerDisposition": "propose-merge-duplicate-into-witnessed-local-person",
      "proposedWitness": {
        "localId": "jiutangshu:153:p044",
        "book": "jiutangshu",
        "chapter": "153",
        "unitId": "s0071",
        "quote": "伯芻"
      },
      "independentVerdict": "hold",
      "primaryWitnessUnits": [
        {
          "unitId": "s0070",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/153.json",
          "zh": "子伯芻。",
          "enLiteral": "His son was Boqu.",
          "enIdiomatic": "His son was Boqu."
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0071",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/153.json",
          "zh": "伯芻，字素芝，登進士第，誌行修謹。",
          "enLiteral": "Boqu, courtesy name Suzhi, passed the jinshi examination; his conduct and aims were cultivated and careful.",
          "enIdiomatic": "Boqu, courtesy name Suzhi, passed the jinshi examination. His conduct was cultivated and careful."
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0083",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/153.json",
          "zh": "伯芻風姿古雅，涉學，善談笑，而動與時適，論者稍薄之。",
          "enLiteral": "Boqu's bearing was ancient and elegant; he was learned and skilled at witty talk, yet his actions often suited the times, and critics slightly looked down on him.",
          "enIdiomatic": "Boqu had an ancient, elegant bearing, was learned, and spoke wittily, yet his actions often suited the moment, and critics held him somewhat lightly."
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0084",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/153.json",
          "zh": "子寬夫，登進士第，歷諸府從事。",
          "enLiteral": "His son Kuanfu passed the jinshi examination and served as staff officer in various offices.",
          "enIdiomatic": "His son Kuanfu passed the jinshi examination and served as staff officer in various provincial offices."
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0097",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/153.json",
          "zh": "寬夫弟端夫，為太常博士，駁韋綬謚議知名。",
          "enLiteral": "Kuanfu's younger brother Duanfu was an Erudite of the Court of Imperial Sacrifices, famous for opposing Wei Shou's posthumous title proposal.",
          "enIdiomatic": "Kuanfu's younger brother Duanfu was an erudite of the Court of Imperial Sacrifices, famous for opposing Wei Shou's posthumous title proposal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caseId": "sha256:e0112e032cc961c807174092de07f893ec2679f57f654966d3bafc7afe07ad96",
      "localId": "jiutangshu:153:p020",
      "canonicalPersonId": "per_TP9MKTK1VZS1SR3CS0QS",
      "transportLocalPeople": [
        "jiutangshu:153:p020"
      ],
      "protectedLocalPeople": [
        "jiutangshu:153:p020"
      ],
      "anchorLocalId": "jiutangshu:153:p020",
      "ownerFinding": "Unnamed inferred placeholder, built on a concrete kinship error. s0026 「高祖武幹」 makes Wu Gan Liu Nai's 高祖, which means great-great-grandfather (父→祖→曾祖→高祖, four generations), not great-grandfather. Two unnamed ancestors therefore stand between Wu Gan and the father 如璠 (s0027), not one \"grandfather\", and neither is quoted. The single grandfather p020 (with its 武德初 AD 618 attestation) misrepresents the chain. Remove p020. Correct claim 143 to 高祖 / great-great-grandfather / generationDistance 4 with intermediary p019 only. Correct p017's descriptive label and English surface. Repair both English fields of s0026 (the definite mistranslation 高祖 → \"great-grandfather\").",
      "ownerDisposition": "accept-hold-propose-remove-inferred-person-and-correct-kinship-generation",
      "independentVerdict": "hold",
      "primaryWitnessUnits": [
        {
          "unitId": "s0026",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/153.json",
          "zh": "高祖武幹，武德初拜侍中，即中書侍郎林甫從祖兄子也。",
          "enLiteral": "His great-grandfather Wu Gan was appointed Palace Attendant at the beginning of Wude; he was the son of the paternal cousin of Zhongshu Vice Director Linpu.",
          "enIdiomatic": "His great-grandfather Wu Gan was made Palace Attendant at the start of the Wude era; he was the son of a paternal cousin of Zhongshu Vice Director Linpu."
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0027",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/153.json",
          "zh": "父如璠，昫山丞，以迺貴，贈民部郎中。",
          "enLiteral": "His father Ru Fan was assistant magistrate of Xushan; because of Nai's eminence he was posthumously made Director in the Ministry of Revenue.",
          "enIdiomatic": "His father Ru Fan had been assistant magistrate of Xushan; because of Nai's eminence he was posthumously made director in the Ministry of Revenue."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
